# 1v1, the field prior on the whole field (BENCH-217, MOVE-35; docs/bench/gun-oracle.md, "K1 step 3"). The danger
# model's first member that carries information no view has: a table of where the field's learning guns put their
# bullets, by the state they aimed at (lateral speed, acceleration, wall room ahead, flight time), fitted offline on
# the oracle's 46,719 bullets from 48 learning guns. It is the last aim member at standing weight 2, scored on the
# bullets that hit us like the aims, so the rolling score weighs it down once the views have learnt this gun.
# Leigh starts it once the PC is free (one card at a time, from master):
#   git checkout master && git pull
#   .\queue.ps1 run pc-field-prior        (or  ./queue.sh run pc-field-prior)
# One bench queue, RoboRumble workers at 0, unpinned, 12 workers, truth log off. Every step resumes; no step needs a
# decision. Size: 1,194 loading robots x 3 arms (c, aa, pf) x 2 seeds = 7,164 battles, ~11 h at ~650 battles/h; the
# pilot (every fifth robot, 1,434 battles, ~2.2 h) comes first and the screen resumes its battles.
#
# Why it should win (the PC card rule of 2026-11-03):
#   - It is the gap the studies found. The replay study (2026-11-07) showed BeepBoop hit 30% less than Hadur by the
#     same guns, from round 1, with the same movement shape: a danger-model gap, not a style gap. The inquisition
#     ledger (2026-11-08) put 63% of all points lost on learning guns over flat movers, the class this member models.
#   - The oracle read, each opponent scored against a table fitted without it: rolling blend +0.386 bits -> +0.440,
#     bullets from the third the surf drives into 7.7% -> 6.8%, 32 of 36 opponents better. In rounds 0-2 the shipped
#     blend scores below a uniform guess (the views are empty; the surf drives on a head-on guess) and the prior takes
#     the leak there from 8-9% to 6-7%. The aim members' step (8.1% -> 7.7%) read +0.07 +- 0.15 APS on these 432
#     guns; this step is three times that size.
#   - Cloud smoke on a census-weighted 49-robot panel (prior-smoke-cloud.txt, 2 seeds from 10600): see
#     docs/bench/local/2026-11-09_prior-smoke.md (filled in before this card runs).
#   - Risk: a wrong prior on a robot whose gun does not shoot like the field is weighed down by its rolling score
#     within a few hits; the member costs 41 kernel sums a wave, nothing against the views' neighbours.
# Pilot (BENCH-218, stop rule): every fifth robot of census-312.txt, less broken-1.11.2.txt's (they have no battles and the pilot analysis refuses an incomplete panel, issue #718; the selection is kept so the first run's battles resume) x c, aa, pf x 2 seeds from 10600. When pf's mean
#   gain over c there is under 0.1 points, work/fpr.stop is written, every later step skips and the results PR carries
#   the pilot alone. The screen resumes the pilot's battles.
# Screen: the whole field x c, aa, pf x 2 seeds from 10600 (multiarm --census for the field read by band).
# Gate: pf against c and aa pooled, field-normalised (shield_s2.py gate --arm pf --bar 0.05, low end above 0, A/A in
#   band, 95% of the panel fought). Also written: per-robot pf-minus-c (per_robot.py) and the 2-point picks
#   (mode_table.py), the fallback if the field read fails but robots win: a per-opponent prior-on line (a later PR).
# Stop rules (docs/bench/watch.md): halt on 30 failed battles, an arm scoring nothing in 8, 90+ skipped turns a battle
# over the last 200, or no battle in 30 minutes; every battle fought is kept and a rerun resumes. Nothing here ships:
# a pass turns MoveDesign.FIELD_PRIOR on by PR; the release rule stands.

set V = 3.21
set P = --parallel 12 --no-truth-log --failed-ok
set C = --skip-build --skip-fetch --rounds 35 --cpu-constant 1488498 --child-heap 2G
set W = work/fpr
set OUT = ../docs/bench/local
set ALERT = lgriffin

prep | git checkout -q master && mkdir -p bisect work && rm -f work/fpr.stop && for a in aa bb pf; do rm -f bisect/hadur117.Hadur_${V}$a.jar; done && bash ./build-ablation.sh aa && bash ./build-ablation.sh bb && bash ./build-ablation.sh fprior && test -f bisect/hadur117.Hadur_${V}aa.jar && test -f bisect/hadur117.Hadur_${V}bb.jar && test -f bisect/hadur117.Hadur_${V}pf.jar && awk 'NR<=2 || (NR>2 && (NR-3)%5==0)' census-312.txt | awk -F'|' '{gsub(/\r/, "")} /^#/ || !NF {next} {n = $1; gsub(/^ +| +$/, "", n); gsub(/ +/, " ", n)} NR == FNR {b[n] = 1; next} !(n in b)' broken-1.11.2.txt - > work/panel-fpr-pilot.txt && ./fetch-opponents.sh --set census-312.txt && mvn -q compile

pilot | ./bench-top20.sh ${C} ${P} --set work/panel-fpr-pilot.txt --seeds 2 --seed-base 10600 --arms plans/field-prior.arms --out ${W} --label fpr --shuffle-jobs && python3 tools/x5_card.py pilot ${W}/arms.tsv --names work/panel-fpr-pilot.txt --check pf=work/panel-fpr-pilot.txt@0.1 --ref c --out ${OUT}/$(date +%Y-%m-%d)_fpr-pilot.md --stop-file work/fpr.stop
  after: prep
  watch: field=1217
  stop: fails 30
  stop: dead 8
  stop: skips 90 over 200
  stop: stall 30m

screen | if [ -f work/fpr.stop ]; then echo 'pilot: pf under 0.1 points over c, no screen'; exit 0; fi && ./bench-top20.sh ${C} ${P} --set census-312.txt --seeds 2 --seed-base 10600 --arms plans/field-prior.arms --out ${W} --label fpr --shuffle-jobs
  after: pilot
  watch: field=1217
  stop: fails 30
  stop: dead 8
  stop: skips 90 over 200
  stop: stall 30m

gate | if [ -f work/fpr.stop ]; then echo 'stopped (see work/fpr.stop): skipped'; exit 0; fi && python3 ../data/tools/multiarm.py ${W}/arms.tsv --census census-312.txt --out ${OUT}/$(date +%Y-%m-%d)_fpr-screen.md && python3 tools/shield_s2.py gate ${W}/arms.tsv --arm pf --panel census-312.txt --bar 0.05 --out ${OUT}/$(date +%Y-%m-%d)_fpr-gate.md && python3 tools/per_robot.py ${W}/arms.tsv --arms pf --out ${OUT}/$(date +%Y-%m-%d)_fpr-per-robot.md --out-tsv ${OUT}/fpr-per-robot.tsv && python3 ../data/tools/mode_table.py ${W}/arms.tsv --margin 2 --out-tsv ${OUT}/fpr-pick.tsv --out ${OUT}/$(date +%Y-%m-%d)_fpr-pick.md
  after: screen

pr | bash tools/open_results_pr.sh claude/pc-field-prior-results "The field prior on the whole field (MOVE-35, BENCH-217)" $(ls ${OUT}/$(date +%Y-%m-%d)_fpr-*.md ${OUT}/fpr-per-robot.tsv ${OUT}/fpr-pick.tsv 2>/dev/null)
  after: gate
